{
  "id": "continuous-performance-test",
  "term": "continuous performance test",
  "definition": "A continuous performance test is a computer-based attention assessment in which a person stays alert for target stimuli within a steady stream of distracting information over a sustained period. It produces measures such as correct detections, omission and commission errors, and reaction time variability, and is often used to help evaluate attention problems, including ADHD.",
